# =============================================
# EngFlow — Environment Variables
# =============================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values
# Never commit .env to the repository

# =============================================
# GitHub
# =============================================

# Your GitHub Personal Access Token
# Generate one at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Required scopes: repo (for private repos) or public_repo (for public only)
GITHUB_TOKEN=your_personal_access_token_here

# Comma-separated list of repos to ingest in the format owner/repo
# Example: GITHUB_REPOS=torvalds/linux,facebook/react
GITHUB_REPOS=owner/repo-name

# =============================================
# Database
# =============================================

# Full Postgres connection string
# Format: postgresql://user:password@host:port/dbname
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/engflow

# =============================================
# Ingestion
# =============================================

# How often to run incremental ingestion, in minutes
INGESTION_SCHEDULE_MINUTES=15

# =============================================
# API
# =============================================

# Port the FastAPI backend will run on
API_PORT=8000

# Environment: development | production
ENVIRONMENT=development

# =============================================
# Frontend
# =============================================

# URL of the FastAPI backend — used by Next.js to make API calls
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
```

A couple of things to do after creating this file:

1. **Duplicate it immediately** — copy it to `.env` and fill in your real values locally
2. **Double check your `.gitignore`** has this line in it:
```
.env